cff-version: 1.2.0

message: "If you use OmniLatent in your research, please cite this repository."

title: "OmniLatent: A Generalizable Multimodal Representation Learning Framework for Biomedical Discovery"

type: software

authors:
  - family-names: "Moafi"
    given-names: "Sepideh"
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher"

url: "https://github.com/AIResearcher20/OmniLatent"

repository-code: "https://github.com/AIResearcher20/OmniLatent"

abstract: >
  OmniLatent is an open-source research framework for multimodal biomedical
  representation learning. The framework integrates heterogeneous biomedical
  data modalities, including molecular and clinical information, into unified
  latent representations for downstream biological and clinical analyses.
  The project focuses on reproducible, interpretable, and generalizable
  representation learning approaches for biomedical discovery.

keywords:
  - multimodal representation learning
  - biomedical AI
  - cancer genomics
  - TCGA
  - deep learning
  - biological interpretability
  - cross-modal alignment
  - open-source scientific software
  - reproducible research

